# Project: TravelAgency
Personal pet project. Repo and wiki are PUBLIC: anything pushed is visible forever.
## Facts
- Repo `PlutoGr/TravelAgency`; wiki = separate repo `TravelAgency.wiki.git`, branch `master`, push = publish.
- Board: GitHub Project (private) «PlutoGr/projects/2». Columns Очередь, В работе, На ревью, Готово.
- Stack: .NET 10 microservices (`src/Services`), gateway, React/TS frontend (`src/Frontend/travel-agency-frontend`, vitest). Tests: `*.UnitTests`, `*.IntegrationTests` (Testcontainers). Follow neighbouring code.
- Single environment: dev (Staging), behind basic auth, self-signed cert. Address and credentials: not in the repo; dev access and server facts come from the lead. Smoke on dev = login, catalog, booking.
- Merge to `main` = automatic deploy to dev («Deploy to dev»). Green CI = `.NET сборка и тесты`, `Фронтенд сборка и тесты`, `gitleaks`.
- Secret values live only on the server `.env`, GitHub Secrets (env `dev`), local `dotnet user-secrets`. Never in the repo.
- Repo wins over any doc; repo `docs/COMMIT_CONVENTION.md` and `.github/pull_request_template.md` win on format conflicts.
## Roles (overrides playbook role names)
| Role | Who | Zone |
|---|---|---|
| Lead / merger | Grok Bot | `.cursor/agents/lead.md`: owner channel, triage, merges, board, approvals routing, server access, audit |
| Architect / reviewer | Вирт (or a cloud agent) | `.cursor/agents/architect.md`: mandatory PR review, architecture, ADR, labels, task split; code only skeletons/contracts |
| Developer | TA Разработчик | app code + tests |
| Tester | TA Тестировщик | tests, bug issues, acceptance on dev |
| DevOps | TA DevOps | CI, Docker, nginx, deploy, server, security check |
| Analyst | TA Продакт-аналитик | wiki, requirements, acceptance criteria |
- Touch only your zone; out of zone, hand over via the issue. Only the lead talks to the owner; team agents never @mention him.
## Priorities
1. Bugs and UX. 2. Profiles. 3. Chat. 4. Aggregation. Analyst orders within this; order changes need the owner.
## Parallel work
- Merge one PR at a time; work may continue: per agent 1 active item + at most 1 waiting.
- Next issue only if it touches no files/endpoints/migrations of an open PR, does not depend on an unmerged PR, and its criteria are final. Branch from fresh `main`.
- Any doubt about overlap: wait or ask the architect. After the previous merge, update the branch before review.
- Returns first (acceptance bug, review changes, new analysis for an item in flight) over new work: bring the current item to a checkpoint (push/comment), then take the return. Analyst keeps at most 2 issues ahead with final criteria.
## Merge order
- Reviewer: Вирт on every PR (incl. impersonal wording, format). Security: DevOps on risky PRs. Merger: Grok Bot, after green CI, review, and Cursor Automations comments per `project-cursor-automations.mdc`; next merge only after «Deploy to dev» is green.
- Dependabot minor/patch: review + CI. Major (e.g. vitest, eslint, jsdom, node majors): also owner approval via the lead.
- Docs-with-code = the matching wiki `Doc-` page.
- Temporary dumps on dev allowed if deleted after the check.
## Cloud agents (project specifics; method in `playbook-cloud-agents.mdc`)
- Developer: all code via a cloud agent, including small fixes. In chat only work needing dev/server access, or small and mid code when the usage mode says so.
- Analyst: any analysis beyond a short answer via a cloud agent on Grok (xhigh for heavy ones): specs, criteria drafts, ADRs, code reading, `Doc-` fact checks, full text of issues and wiki edits (returned as ready Russian text). In chat: briefs, coordination, posting, small fixes.
- Tester: acceptance on dev stays in chat (needs dev access); API/curl first, browser only for what must be seen, batch several issues per deploy. Automated tests via a cloud agent when an issue needs them.
- DevOps: server stays in chat; a cloud agent may edit workflows or Dockerfiles, DevOps checks the diff.
- Architect: review per `.cursor/agents/architect.md`.
- Launch: repo `https://github.com/PlutoGr/TravelAgency`, title with the issue number, branch `<role>/<NN>-<slug>`; announce one line to the team: `#NN: cloud agent <id>, <model> <params>`.
- Gates after a cloud agent: architect review, green CI, DevOps on risky PRs, merge by the lead, acceptance on dev. Cloud agents never touch the wiki, the board or merges.
- Usage mode and budgets: ask the lead (it keeps them current).
